1
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:03,530
Hot dogs. I love hot dogs.

2
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:06,530
There is nothing better than a hot dog in the country.

3
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:08,530
Hot dogs and mustard.

4
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:10,530
Cooked outdoors over an open fire.

5
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:12,530
I wish I had one now.

6
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:16,530
Do you remember when Daddy and I used to take you

7
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:19,530
and Susan and Robbie to Jones Beach? Susan Roobbie

8
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:20,530
Oh, I sure do.

9
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:22,530
We'd wait until dark and make a fire,

10
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:24,530
and we'd cook the hot dogs.

11
00:02:24,530 --> 00:02:28,530
Oh, don't forget the mustard.

12
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:30,530
And, oh, does anybody want ketchup?

13
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:32,530
I might as well take it along.

14
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:35,530
And now to make sure we've got the hamburger patties.

15
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:45,530
I have to remember to put them in the bag

16
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:47,530
tomorrow morning before we leave.

17
00:02:47,530 --> 00:02:49,530
I'll remind you, Richard.

18
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:52,530
Mom,

19
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:54,530
we really appreciate your taking care of Max for the weekend

20
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:56,530
and giving up your free time.

21
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:58,530
I love doing it.

22
00:02:58,530 --> 00:03:00,530
Susan and Harry have a sitter for Michelle in the city, Susan

23
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:04,530
and I'm taking care of Max.

24
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:05,530
It's no big deal.

25
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:06,530
I am happy to do it for you.

26
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:08,530
I guess Max is asleep by now.

27
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:10,530
He's not crying anymore.

28
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:12,530
Oh, poor baby. He's teething.

29
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:14,530
Well, he's asleep--finally.

30
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:17,530
I feel so bad for him.

31
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:21,530
It hurts so much when a baby gets his first teeth.

32
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:24,530
He'll be fine, Marilyn.

33
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,530
Well, he wakes up several times during the night,

34
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:27,530
and the pain is so bad.

35
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:30,530
I'm really concerned about going away for the weekend, Ellen,

36
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:33,530
and leaving you with the full responsibility of taking care of Max.

37
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:35,530
Especially with his teething.

38
00:03:35,530 --> 00:03:36,530
I wish he felt better.

39
00:03:36,530 --> 00:03:38,530
Please don't worry, Marilyn.

40
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:40,530
Remember your father-in-law's a pediatrician.

41
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:44,530
We have a live-in doctor if there's a problem I can't handle.

42
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:45,530
I agree, Marilyn.

43
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:47,530
We really don't have to be overly concerned.

44
00:03:47,530 --> 00:03:53,530
I'll go upstairs and stay with him until he falls asleep again.

45
00:03:53,530 --> 00:03:55,530
Thanks, Richard.

46
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:59,530
Try putting him across your lap on his stomach.

47
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,530
He likes that.

48
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:02,530
I'll try it.

49
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:05,530
When are Susan and Harry picking you up, Marilyn? Susan

50
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:07,530
They're coming by at six tomorrow morning,

51
00:04:07,530 --> 00:04:09,530
so we can get an early start.

52
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:10,530
That's nice.

53
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:12,530
And you'll have a full day in the country.

54
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:13,530
And a full night.

55
00:04:13,530 --> 00:04:16,530
Tomorrow night we'll be camping out in tents.

56
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,530
And coming home on Sunday?

57
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:22,530
We'll be heading back late in the afternoon.

58
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:26,530
You're going to have the time of your lives.

59
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:29,530
Camping out is such great fun.

60
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:32,530
We'll have a great time camping out, I'm sure.

61
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:35,530
But I'm still a little worried about you, Ellen.

62
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:37,530
It will be my great pleasure, Marilyn.

63
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:40,530
Remember, it's only one night.

64
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,530
He's asleep.

65
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:45,530
I think he'll sleep through the night now.

66
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:46,530
Thanks, honey.

67
00:04:46,530 --> 00:04:49,530
I hope he's good when we're away.

68
00:04:49,530 --> 00:04:52,530
Well, so do I.

69
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:55,530
Now, to check the list of things we need for the camping trip.

70
00:04:55,530 --> 00:04:59,530
We need to bring a flashlight.

71
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:03,530
It's in the right-hand drawer, next to the bottle openers.

72
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:08,530
Do we have a bottle opener on the list, Marilyn?

73
00:05:08,530 --> 00:05:14,530
No. No bottle opener.

74
00:05:14,530 --> 00:05:17,530
Is that one of the things Susan and Harry are bringing?

75
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:19,530
No.

76
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:22,530
And we're bringing the ketchup, mustard, relish--all that stuff.

77
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,530
And cooking utensils.

78
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:28,530
Well, here's the bottle opener, and here's the flashlight.

79
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:31,530
Matches.

80
00:05:31,530 --> 00:05:32,530
Matches.

81
00:05:32,530 --> 00:05:33,530
Yes, of course.

82
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:35,530
For when we build our campfire.

83
00:05:35,530 --> 00:05:39,530
I can't build a fire by rubbing two pieces of wood together.

84
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:42,530
And don't forget your camera and film, Richard.

85
00:05:42,530 --> 00:05:43,530
All packed and ready.

86
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:46,530
And let's not forget our cassette player and some tapes.

87
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:48,530
Some music tapes and some blank tapes

88
00:05:48,530 --> 00:05:51,530
so that we can record our thoughts about the trip.

89
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:53,530
Oh, that's a nice idea.

90
00:05:53,530 --> 00:05:55,530
An audio diary.

91
00:05:55,530 --> 00:05:56,530
That's what I thought.

92
00:05:56,530 --> 00:05:58,530
Got it!

93
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:01,530
The cassette player and the tapes.
